Despite dropping the entire set of address hash keys (~`150GB` index) in favor of dynamic in-place hashing over the full script , the queries are still fast. The large address query takes `8.5ms` (data), `10ms` (text), and `13.7ms` (json). This returns an array of `7,453` serialized output points:
```[
  {
    "point": {
      "hash": "db9847575ef720b8b5582bac74bcedef1b6a08903ddc27638024b8d0d3ba0400",
      "index": 0
    },
    "value": 1270486495
  },
  ...
]```
